A||||4||Matt88||88 rear calipers||||1||
Z||000000||Matt88||02-19-2001||03:40 PM||||Thought I would save some money and replace the rear brake pads myself.  The Haynes manual says to take out the 2 way check valve to see if there are any leaks and then replace it with a new one.<P>Do not touch this part unless you want to buy a caliper rebuild kit ($38 each!)  The part isn't available separately.  My valve, which is only a simple rubber plug probably worth about .03, fell appart due to age, etc.  I had no brake fluid leakage from the piston seal so I didn't plan on a rebuild - I guess I am now.<P>I bought my rebuild kit from the local Pontiac dealer (the kit from Schucks didn't have the valve) for $38 plus $5 shipping (can you say special order?)  <P>Does any one know if the kit from the Fiero Store contain the 2 way valve?  Their kit is about $10 cheaper.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||02-19-2001||04:10 PM||||It does on the 88 rebuild kit. If in doubt call them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||02-20-2001||12:52 AM||||I can verify... the check valve is included.  Get the Fiero Store kit.<P>I think your just as well off rebuilding those suckers anyway... as long as its all apart.  I did my rear brakes last year... bottomed the pistons and put it back together.  I was quickly sorry that I didn't rebuild because both pistons began to leak.  The old rubber seals inside didn't survive bottoming the piston, so I had to rebuild them anyway.  I did use the Fiero Store kit and had no problems.  GRRR I hate the 88 calipers!  Good luck!! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Matt88||02-20-2001||03:28 PM||||Thanks for the info.  <P>Yea, I'm going to rebuild both calipers anyway - now that I have to buy one rebuild kit, I might as well do both.<P>Do the words "think ahead" ring a bell for anyone?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||02-20-2001||06:44 PM||||If you are going to just rebuild the caliber you can save money and buy a rebuild kit for the front. That is less than $4 at Autozone. That kit only has the outside dust boot and the caliber seal. It is the same size as the rear caliber. ||||reg||1
